# Cloudflare Workers static-asset redirects. Wrangler reads this from public/
# (Hugo copies it out of static/). Path rules only: the apex -> www host
# redirect cannot be expressed here and lives in a Cloudflare Redirect Rule on
# the zone. See docs/deployment/cloudflare.md.
#
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom, first match wins, so specific rules go
# above the wildcards that would otherwise swallow them.

# Retired Spotify content adaptor, and the per-artist pages beneath it.
/projects/content-adaptors/spotify/ /listening/artists/ 301
/projects/content-adaptors/spotify/* /listening/artists/:splat 301

# Retired paginated artist index. /listening/artists/ used to be a 24-per-page
# grid (/listening/artists/page/2/ ... /page/40/) and is now a single cloud, so
# those URLs no longer exist. :n matches one path segment, so this covers every
# page number without listing them. No artist lives at /listening/artists/page/<x>/
# (artist URLs have no sub-path), so nothing real can be caught. Page 1 only ever
# duplicated the index root, so it goes there; deeper pages went to long-tail
# artists, so they go to the full A-Z. Keep these: docs/seo/invariants.md.
/listening/artists/page/1/ /listening/artists/ 301
/listening/artists/page/:n/ /listening/a-z/ 301

# Old hiking-guide URL. It used to be only a Hugo alias (meta refresh), and
# Google kept the stub indexed five months on, ranking it at 6.26, above the
# real page at 6.74. Leave the alias in content/trails/bluff-creek-trail/index.md
# until this rule is confirmed live; drop it only after that.
/projects/hiking/westchester-playa-vista-playa-del-rey-hiking-guide/bluff-creek-trail/ /trails/bluff-creek-trail/ 301
